('CHE_Z_02','Chemistry','Z','K2','Chemical Changes','If you leave an iron cutlass outside in the rain, it rusts. How does the weight of the rusty cutlass compare to when it was new?','[{"id":"a","text":"It is lighter because the rust eats away the iron.","points":1},{"id":"b","text":"It is exactly the same weight, just a different color.","points":0},{"id":"c","text":"It is heavier because oxygen from the air has combined with the iron.","points":5},{"id":"d","text":"It is lighter because water washed away the metal.","points":0}]'::jsonb,null,null,null,'["Reading Comprehension","Logical Deduction"]'::jsonb,1),
