('CHE_C_01','Chemistry','C','K1','Equilibrium','In a sealed, dynamic equilibrium system (A + B ⇌ C + D), what happens if you add more of substance A?','[{"id":"a","text":"The reaction stops completely.","points":0},{"id":"b","text":"The system shifts to produce more C and D to re-balance.","points":5},{"id":"c","text":"The system shifts to produce more B.","points":1},{"id":"d","text":"Nothing happens because it is already balanced.","points":0}]'::jsonb,null,null,null,'["Reading Comprehension","Spatial Reasoning"]'::jsonb,2),
('CHE_C_02','Chemistry','C','K2','Intermolecular Forces','Water (H2O) boils at 100°C, while Methane (CH4) boils at -161°C, even though they are similar in size. Why?','[{"id":"a","text":"Water has stronger covalent bonds inside the molecule.","points":1},{"id":"b","text":"Water molecules form strong hydrogen bonds WITH EACH OTHER, requiring more energy to separate them.","points":5},{"id":"c","text":"Methane is a gas by nature, so it doesn''t need heat.","points":0},{"id":"d","text":"Water is heavier.","points":0}]'::jsonb,null,null,null,'["Spatial Reasoning"]'::jsonb,2),
('CHE_C_03','Chemistry','C','K3','Limiting Reactants','To make one bicycle, you need 1 frame and 2 wheels. If you have 5 frames and 8 wheels, how many bicycles can you make, and what is the limiting "reactant"?','[{"id":"a","text":"5 bicycles, limiting is wheels.","points":0},{"id":"b","text":"4 bicycles, limiting is wheels.","points":5},{"id":"c","text":"4 bicycles, limiting is frames.","points":1},{"id":"d","text":"8 bicycles, limiting is frames.","points":0}]'::jsonb,null,null,null,'["Spatial Reasoning","Graph Illiteracy"]'::jsonb,1),
